BOUND IDENTIFIERS AND ACTION ROUTES
The service-location exception concerns a named city or calling region in
otherwise equivalent service prose. It never covers a literal address or URL
used to submit, pay or perform an account action. The actual action route must
itself be preserved, even when its spelling contains the permitted city name
and all surrounding instructions match. An analogous route is not coverage.
Likewise, the subject of an actual failed-object/status/permission assertion
is a bound record identity, not an unpopulated query or navigation control.
Apply the control exception only after distinguishing these actual assertions.

INTERFACE VALUES AND LIST COVERAGE
Classify the visible role before treating a number, name, date or version as a
record fact. A search input, selectable facet, sort choice, archive link or
documentation version selector navigates content; its value does not assert
the unseen content. When the displayed actual results and substantive text
are fully preserved, changed control values, facet subsets and their counts
are harmless UI. A version selector alone does not provide a changed API,
command, compatibility requirement or version-specific explanation. A search
word in introductory tool copy is not an actual example sentence or result.
Do not infer unshown records, behavior or facts from controls or headings.

Actual populated records remain protected: changed people/items in a result,
prices, measurements, availability, event timing, API facts and real status or
permission assertions are material. A record identifier in 'object X failed'
is the subject of an actual assertion, unlike a query box value. An actual
submission/payment/account endpoint is an action destination, not navigation.
Incidental citation-access/publication metadata can be harmless when the same
work and all substantive terms survive; dates in the work or event are facts.

A broader list can replace a filtered subset only when it preserves every
actual item and its price, availability and conditions. A narrower filter or
displayed count alone adds no uncovered item fact. If the broader list adds a
useful item, only the covering direction is allowed. Conflicting actual facts
and new record details still require retention. A full shared policy/message
can be a retained basis; common navigation alone is insufficient.

